reviews.remaining:
Open against the frozen Hermes contract:
(1) per-job isolated model workdir/skills/project-instruction context (only the script-only no_agent workdir is supported);
(2) a Cron page aggregating jobs across all profiles (cross-profile);
(3) schedule.create, the model-callable scheduling grant with its governance policy that the original requires (a protected root outside this scope);
(4) native mobile job surfaces and authoring;
(5) delegation and dynamic plugin tool groups in the scheduled enabled_toolsets catalog (only basic/files/terminal and the curated execute_code group exist, with nested file/web RPC restricted by the same scheduled bound), and their transitive restriction contracts.
Options without a runtime are refused, not saved inert. There is no live proof for the scheduler, channels or native mobile authoring; monitors depend on the configured sources and do not install integrations. Cloud pins must match existing policy routing; changed local models require loaded context metadata, and LM Studio currently cannot resolve a changed model. Pinned jobs use deterministic compression and omit auxiliary embedding recall.

