A hostname-parsed protocol table guards every model backend at the wire. host_mandated_protocol (agents/core/llm/host_protocol.py:112) takes the hostname from hostname_of (agents/core/llm/host_protocol.py:85). hostname_of parses strings with httpx.URL, the parser the wire dials with (agents/core/llm/host_protocol.py:103). A fullwidth, ideographic or halfwidth-ideographic dot spelling of a vendor host is therefore refused at HybridRouter.detect() as well as at the wire. urlsplit remains the fallback for text httpx rejects, and httpx cannot dial that text either. The host is lower-cased with the trailing dot dropped, then matched exactly or as whole labels (agents/core/llm/host_protocol.py:62-69): api.anthropic.com -> anthropic_messages; api.openai.com and one regional label -> openai; bedrock-runtime[-fips].<region>.amazonaws.com[.cn] -> bedrock_converse. Lookalike suffixes, path spoofs and userinfo spoofs mandate nothing. Each backend's ledger name declares its protocol (agents/core/llm/host_protocol.py:49). The declared llm_async_client callers on this head are anthropic, gemini (gemini_cache included), openai-responses, xai, openrouter, lm-studio (agents/core/llm/base.py:594), ollama (agents/core/llm/base.py:911), vlm and the approval judge's openai-compatible; the undeclared client names that also exist on this head (deepinfra in deepinfra.py and vision_deepinfra.py, nous and nous-metadata, models-dev, and vlm's provider_id variants) speak no declared protocol, so protocol_refusal refuses them on every mandated vendor host (agents/core/llm/host_protocol.py:141-146) and they can only reach unmandated hosts. The synchronous embedding clients (llm_sync_client and llm_sync_request_hook, agents/core/llm/egress.py:113-142: ollama, lm-studio) run the same protocol_refusal check. protocol_refusal (agents/core/llm/host_protocol.py:131) also refuses an undeclared backend on a mandated host. The check lives in the egress-ledger request hook that every backend's llm_async_client carries (agents/core/llm/egress.py:76-79), so it runs on every redirect hop. A mismatch records an allowed=False ledger row with the reason and raises before the transport is touched, so neither the body nor the auth header leaves. HybridRouter.detect refuses a compatible base URL on a host that mandates another protocol (agents/core/llm/hybrid_router.py:394); the refusal is logged and the backend is not built. HostProtocolRefused subclasses Exception, neither OSError nor httpx.HTTPError (agents/core/llm/host_protocol.py:73), so no connection-failure handler reads a refusal as 'backend down'. OllamaBackend.resolve_context_window logs a warning and returns unknown on a refusal (agents/core/llm/base.py:933), instead of raising out of compaction and route planning. Adaptation from Hermes: Nerva has no per-session api_mode that can go stale, so the mandate refuses a mismatched backend rather than re-picking a protocol. Nerva's OpenAI family admits both OpenAI dialects (chat completions and Responses) at api.openai.com. Base URLs remain env-only until the named-custom-endpoints row exists, and the wire guard covers any base URL unchanged. Coverage is tests/test_host_mandated_protocol.py (43 tests):
- vendor hosts, including the 5 IDNA-dot spellings (tests/test_host_mandated_protocol.py:61);
- 15 lookalike, path, userinfo and other hosts (tests/test_host_mandated_protocol.py:82);
- an OpenAI-protocol backend aimed at api.anthropic.com sends zero requests and leaves two blocked ledger rows (tests/test_host_mandated_protocol.py:119);
- the client raises before dispatch (tests/test_host_mandated_protocol.py:141);
- matching and unmandated hosts still flow (tests/test_host_mandated_protocol.py:151);
- a redirect onto a vendor host is refused per hop (tests/test_host_mandated_protocol.py:164);
- router refusals, including both IDNA spellings (tests/test_host_mandated_protocol.py:204, tests/test_host_mandated_protocol.py:213, tests/test_host_mandated_protocol.py:234);
- the default and custom endpoints are still built (tests/test_host_mandated_protocol.py:222);
- the refusal is neither an OSError nor an httpx.HTTPError (tests/test_host_mandated_protocol.py:247);
- the Ollama probe degrades and leaves a blocked ledger row (tests/test_host_mandated_protocol.py:254).
