  - both CLI flags (tests/test_job_first_run.py:353, tests/test_job_first_run.py:363).
- tests/test_nerva_cli.py:1571 and tests/test_slash_commands.py:373.
- frontend/src/test/jobs-first-run.test.ts (armNote).
- tests/test_jobs_routes.py: a new reminder still sends nothing until /run, and the script job's /run is again a fresh manual request.
Every guard added in the second review was mutated out one at a time, and a test failed each time. 656 job, dispatch, command, CLI and schedule tests pass.

One-shot run_at jobs (H450) never take a first run, even when one is asked for: first_run_policy and first_run_decision answer "one-shot" (agents/core/autonomy/jobs.py:602, :607). The H450 row says they must stay out of the first run. A known pre-existing gap outside this row: parse_schedule drops a window or day qualifier after an interval ("every 30 minutes between 9 and 17" becomes '*/30 * * * *'), so such a job runs all day and counts as an interval. Image-recovery collateral review (2026-10-02): changes to shared CLI/image-turn or HUD local-panel disclosure are outside this row's claimed symbols. Complete base evidence pins and unchanged text anchors verified; existing capability/status preserved. Claim-specific source inspection is recorded in the bounded image source review.

